cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below and the accompanying paper, \"Comparing protein conformational ensembles across sequences and lengths\" (manuscript)."
title: "framedchain: framed chains for protein structures and ensembles of any length"
version: 0.4.3
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23911383
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: "Framed chains: a metric space for protein structures and ensembles of any length. Each virtual Calpha-Calpha bond becomes a 3x3 matrix, the orthonormal frame of the bond and its peptide plane scaled by bond length; an absent bond is the zero matrix. The package computes the order-preserving edit-distance metric across lengths with branch-and-bound certification, its exact split into shared-bond and unshared-bond parts, mean points and geodesics, and energy statistics for ensembles."
authors:
  - family-names: "An"
    given-names: "Hyeonsu"
    affiliation: "Department of Applied Artificial Intelligence, Sungkyunkwan University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5636-772X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gaony571/framedchain"
keywords:
  - framed chains
  - protein structure
  - metric
  - structural alignment
  - molecular dynamics ensembles
  - energy distance
